	Stevens VAXCluster node SITVXA.  Running VAX/VMS version 5.5-2.
        For general VAXcluster information, type:       $ HELP OVERVIEW

	Unauthorized use is not allowed; keystroke monitoring by 
	authorized personnel may be in effect when system security or 
	integrity is in question.  By using this system, you expressly 
	consent to such monitoring and any resultant legal actions.
 
	
    Last interactive login on Monday,  8-NOV-1993 [xxxx-cmk]
    Last non-interactive login on Monday,  8-NOV-1993 [xxxx-cmk]
Messages to users can be read in BULLETIN Utility; type BULLETIN at "$" prompt.
        ANTI-WATCHDOG programs are prohibited on the VAXcluster.
  See the consultants, Rm. 31, Computer Ctr., in person for dial-up numbers.

	Look for the Computer Center Fall Seminar Schedule in BULLETIN.
+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
The Computer Center's next seminar "Network Commands", will take place on Wed.
Nov.10 in the 5th floor Conference Room (Stevens Center Bldg.) from 3:00-4:00. 
Some of the commands Chris Hose will cover are: FTP,TELNET, COPY,and SEND/FILE.
++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
Sending electronic mail or messages to other users at Stevens (or elsewhere)
UNDER A PHONEY USERNAME is not permitted.  Having mail-sending programs which 
falsify the sender's identity is also not allowed since this type of program 
is only "useful" for sending phoney mail.  
++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
	Sending "chain" letters is not permitted on Stevens campus
	network or externally out across Internet, BITNET, etc.
	This is considered a serious offense by the guidelines of
	the Network Review Board.  Violators are subject to loss
	of access to the academic VAXcluster pending deliberation/decision
	by the Network Review Board (student policy-enforcing group.)
	If you receive chain mail, *do not* pass it on to others.
